 "notes": [
  "expected_bill_usd: expected annual crop-insurance drought indemnity at today's insured acres and 2020-2024 average liability per acre; lo/hi from 100 block-bootstrap refits.",
  "taxpayer_share_usd = federal premium subsidy share (2020-2024) x expected bill; lo/hi scale the bill interval by the same fraction.",
  "actual_2022_usd / actual_2023_usd: RMA drought indemnity for the principal crops (nominal).",
  "change_2045_pct: NEX-GDDP-CMIP6 2035-2054 vs 1995-2014 deltas applied to NASA POWER weather; est = median over GCMs x two soil-moisture assumptions (root-zone wetness shifted by the NASA POWER emulator, or held at observed); lo/hi = 5th-95th percentile over GCM x soil assumption x bootstrap draws.",
  "diversity_savings_usd: expected annual bill reduction if every county's share of cropland in 3+ crop rotations rose to at least the regional insured-acre-weighted 90th percentile; Scenario assumption, not an estimate from the county data: field trials (Bowles et al. 2020) found 14-90% smaller maize drought-year yield losses in diversified rotations. est = trial lower bound (14%); lo = no effect (the county data show no robust effect); hi = trial upper bound (90%)."
 ]
}